{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}{{ view.entry.name }} — Data maps{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
{% macro hop_label(hop) %}{{ hop.hop }}{% if hop.location %}: {{ hop.location }}{% endif %}{% if hop.device %}: {{ hop.device }}{% endif %}{% if hop.name %}: {{ hop.name }}{% endif %}{% if hop.data_stream %}: {{ hop.data_stream }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro hop_strip(hops) %}
{% for hop in hops %}
<span class="hop hop-{{ hop.hop }}">{{ hop_label(hop) }}</span>
{% if not loop.last %}<span class="route-arrow">&rarr;</span>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% set ns = namespace(detailed=false) %}
{% for hop in hops %}{% if hop.constraints or hop.notes %}{% set ns.detailed = true %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% if ns.detailed %}
<details class="panel route-detail">
<summary>Route detail</summary>
<dl class="hop-list">
{% for hop in hops %}{% if hop.constraints or hop.notes %}
<dt>{{ hop_label(hop) }}</dt>
<dd>{% if hop.constraints %}<p class="hop-constraints"><strong>Constraints:</strong> {{ hop.constraints }}</p>{% endif %}{% if hop.notes %}<p class="hop-notes">{{ hop.notes }}</p>{% endif %}</dd>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
</dl>
</details>
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
<section class="tech-header">
<h2>{{ view.entry.name }}{% if view.draft %} <span class="badge badge-draft">DRAFT — verify against vendor docs</span>{% endif %}</h2>
<p class="meta">{{ view.entry.vendor }}{% if view.doc.versions %} · {{ view.doc.versions }}{% endif %} · <span class="badge badge-status-{{ view.entry.status }}">{{ view.entry.status }}</span> · <a href="../exports/{{ view.entry.id }}.json">JSON export</a> · <a href="../studio/#/tech/{{ view.entry.id }}">Edit in Studio</a></p>
<div class="side-toggle" id="side-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Route portrayal">
<span class="side-label">Route portrayal:</span>
<button type="button" data-side="guarded" class="active">guarded — crosses Everfox HSG</button>
<button type="button" data-side="direct">direct — high-side</button>
</div>
{% if view.format_choice %}
<details class="panel" id="export-choice">
<summary>Export format choice across this technology</summary>
{% if view.format_choice.universal %}
<table><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Alerting fields satisfied</th><th>Datasets offering it</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for row in view.format_choice.rows %}
<tr><td class="mono">{{ row.format }}</td><td>{{ row.required_mapped }}</td><td>{{ row.datasets_offering }}{% if row.datasets_missing %} <span class="missing">({{ row.datasets_missing }} without)</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
{% else %}
<p>No single format is offered by every dataset here, so this technology has no one-export-config choice to make.</p>
{% endif %}
</details>
{% endif %}
{% if view.doc.references %}
<ul class="refs">
{% for ref in view.doc.references %}
<li>{{ ref }}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}
<details class="panel page-help">
<summary>How to read this page</summary>
<ul class="help-list">
<li><strong>DRAFT badge</strong> &mdash; the map is researched from vendor documentation but not yet verified against the deployed system. Confirm before building detections on it.</li>
<li><strong>Route portrayal toggle</strong> &mdash; this technology has instances in both enclaves, and each side describes a separate feed, not a configuration choice: <em>guarded</em> is the low-side feed that crosses the Everfox guard on its way to Elastic; <em>direct</em> is the high-side feed that never crosses. Your choice sticks as you move between pages. A dataset marked <em>no CDS crossing</em> exists only on the high side and shows a single route.</li>
<li><strong>Route strip</strong> &mdash; the pipeline path hop by hop. Each chip is a pipeline tier (source device, edge Cribl worker group, guard, core Cribl worker group, Elastic data stream), never a hostname. A chip labelled <em>other</em> is a tier outside the Cribl/guard/Elastic vocabulary and names itself &mdash; a vendor-owned collector or a cluster the product writes to directly.</li>
<li><strong>Route detail</strong> &mdash; expands the strip above it into per-hop prose, in route order, for the side you have selected. A guard hop carries its <em>Constraints</em> line: what the crossing policy permits for this feed, or that the policy is still open with the guard owner. Other hops explain how the data reaches the next tier.</li>
<li><strong>Format buttons</strong> (when a dataset has more than one) &mdash; the wire formats the vendor can emit, each carrying its score as satisfied/total required fields. The one marked <em>recommended</em> is the best-covering format &mdash; usually the one with the highest score, and where scores tie the order is a non-empty field inventory first, then an entry a parser already exists for (an Elastic integration or a Cribl pack) over one that needs a pipeline written, then the higher total mapped-field count, then the order the formats are declared in; a documented override can name a different format instead, and a dataset with only one format is recommended by default. The recommended format is the one counted in coverage numbers and named as the recommendation in the exports, while the rest are documented alternates for migration planning &mdash; the ECS index counts a usage for every format and flags the recommended one, so an alternate's fields are findable there too. When an override is in effect, a <strong>Recommended</strong> note under the format explains why the highest-scoring format was passed over. A <strong>Switching to&hellip;</strong> line under the coverage line names any alternate format that would satisfy more alerting-required fields than the recommended one, and lists which fields. Everything below the buttons &mdash; parsing, recommendations, coverage, and the field table &mdash; belongs to the selected format.</li>
<li><strong>Enable note</strong> &mdash; how or when a format other than the recommended one is turned on, on the vendor side.</li>
<li><strong>Parsing chip</strong> &mdash; the mechanism that structures the data (Elastic integration, Cribl pack or pipeline, Elastic ingest pipeline), followed by the named artifact.</li>
<li><strong>Recommendation block</strong> &mdash; the migration work for the side you have selected. The <em>parse</em> chip states where parsing happens in the pipeline: <em>low</em> is near the source, <em>high</em> is near Elastic, <em>hybrid</em> splits the work, and the small tag beside it reads <em>doctrine</em> when that location follows the standing parse-placement rule for this mechanism, or <em>judgment</em> when an author set it by hand and doctrine has no opinion; when the author's placement disagrees with what the rule would have picked, the tag is highlighted and reads <em>doctrine says &hellip;</em>, naming the location the rule settles on instead. <em>Cribl</em> and <em>Elastic</em> lines carry each team's work; the <em>Relay</em> line appears only on the guarded side and covers what this feed needs from the guard crossing.</li>
<li><strong>Coverage line</strong> &mdash; how many alerting-required ECS fields the selected format satisfies, then total fields mapped.</li>
<li><strong>Export format choice</strong> &mdash; when the technology's datasets offer more than one export format between them, this panel lists any format offered by every dataset here, with the alerting fields it satisfies and how many datasets offer it, so a single export configuration can be chosen technology-wide; if no format is universal, the panel says so.</li>
<li><strong>Field table</strong> &mdash; the vendor's documented fields and their ECS homes. <em>ECS</em> is the standard target; <em>Custom</em> is the fallback namespace when no ECS home exists. <em>Status</em> describes the field's relationship to ECS: <em>mapped</em> is a clean ECS home, usable as documented; <em>partial</em> means that relationship is incomplete and the Transform note says how &mdash; either an ECS target that needs a caveat or conversion, or <em>no</em> ECS target but a real obligation still attached (a value to split, branch on, or derive an ECS field from, or one deliberately withheld from an ECS field for a documented reason); <em>unmapped</em> lives in a custom namespace with no ECS work outstanding. A dot in <em>Alerting</em> means a CSOC alerting profile requires that ECS field &mdash; derived automatically from the profiles, never hand-authored.</li>
<li><strong>No field table</strong> &mdash; on an alternate format this is deliberate, not an error, and the line states the reason for that format: commonly the vendor publishes its field inventory only behind a support login, the keys are an operator-defined template rather than a fixed vendor list, or the format re-serializes the fields another entry on this dataset already inventories. An alternate format with neither a table nor that line is an authoring gap and is flagged on the catalog page.</li>
<li><strong>Example record</strong> &mdash; a real record captured from the deployed feed, published byte-for-byte. The summary carries its label and size; the block opens on request and stays closed when the page is printed. Large records are shown truncated inline and the download link always serves every byte. A dataset with no example block simply has no record captured yet.</li>
</ul>
</details>
</section>
<div id="tech-page" class="side-guarded">
{% for ds in view.datasets %}
<section class="dataset" id="ds-{{ ds.data.id }}">
<h3>{{ ds.data.name }}
{% for cat in ds.data.event_categories %}<span class="chip chip-cat">{{ cat }}</span>{% endfor %}
{% if not ds.data.route.guarded %}<span class="chip chip-nocds">no CDS crossing</span>{% endif %}
</h3>
{% if ds.data.description %}<p>{{ ds.data.description }}</p>{% endif %}
{% if ds.data.route.guarded %}
<div class="route route-guarded">{{ hop_strip(ds.data.route.guarded) }}</div>
<div class="route route-direct">{{ hop_strip(ds.data.route.direct) }}</div>
{% else %}
<div class="route">{{ hop_strip(ds.data.route.direct) }}</div>
{% endif %}
{% if ds.formats|length > 1 %}
<div class="format-switch" role="group" aria-label="Vendor export format">
{% for fv in ds.formats %}
<button type="button" data-format="{{ fv.data.format }}"{% if fv.recommended %} class="active"{% endif %}>{{ fv.data.format }}{% if fv.recommended %} · recommended{% endif %} <span class="fmt-score">{{ fv.required_mapped|length }}/{{ fv.required|length }}</span></button>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}
{% for fv in ds.formats %}
<div class="format-variant{% if fv.recommended %} active{% endif %}" data-format="{{ fv.data.format }}">
{% include "_format_block.html.j2" %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
{% if ds.examples %}
<div class="examples">
{% for ex in ds.examples %}
<details class="panel example">
<summary>{% if ex.root == "samples" %}Sample record{% else %}Example record{% endif %} &mdash; {{ ex.label }} &middot; {{ ex.size }} bytes</summary>
{% if ex.truncated %}
<p class="example-truncated">Shown truncated &mdash; download the full record.</p>
{% endif %}
<pre class="example-body">{{ ex.text }}</pre>
{% if ex.source %}
<p class="example-source">Source: <a href="{{ ex.source.repo }}">{{ ex.source.repo | replace("https://github.com/", "") }}</a> @ <code>{{ ex.source.commit[:12] }}</code>{% for p in ex.source.paths %} &middot; <a href="{{ ex.source.repo }}/blob/{{ ex.source.commit }}/{{ p }}">{{ p.split("/")[-1] }}</a>{% endfor %} &mdash; {{ ex.source.license }} (<a href="{{ asset_prefix }}{{ ex.root }}/NOTICE.md">notice</a>)</p>
{% endif %}
<p><a class="example-download" href="{{ asset_prefix }}{{ ex.root or "examples" }}/{{ ex.relpath }}">Download raw record</a></p>
</details>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}
</section>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endblock %}
